o our like patio  which then kind of gave him the idea of  like oh outside is where i go to potty  and then we just kind of went for it and  took away the potty pads totally uh and  then he was potty trained but it took a  very long time i just remember those  first like few months i was like i feel  like i'm living in a stye of poo and pee  ellie on the other hand we got her when  she was six months old and so she was a  little bit she had more like bladder  control and so it was a little easier to  potty train her she was also very  responsive so i think it maybe took like  a month maybe to get her used to going  outside and for that we we did use potty  pads but really what we did was every  hour we would take her out and if she  partied outside we would reward her for  it so we did kind of two very different  methods for our dogs and we did  something that works for both of them  just based on what they were used to  prior and their age  next question is about how do you deal  with shedding which yeah dog shed  i don't honestly mind it because my  beagle that i grew up with shed so i'm  like used to it as like a lifestyle  thing it's okay that there's dog hair in  places like my hair is also in places  but yeah it's it's a lot and so some of  the things that we've done to help us is  to number one get a really good vacuum  number two get a really good wet vacuum  and number three get stuff that you can  machine wash okay the next big question  that i got a bunch of times was about  training which all of these things about  lifestyle changes and stuff like can  really all be managed and mitigated with  proper training and then the second kind  of meta question that i got with this is  like should i put my dog in training is  it actually necessary i'm gonna say if  this is your first time taking care of a  dog then absolutely yes it's really  helpful to put your dog in training not  to train your dog but to train yourself  to learn how to train a dog because the  most important thing is to set up a way  to communicate between yourself and the  dog like they're not people so they  don't understand words inherently like  we do and so it's a lot about learning  how to cue them how to motivate them how  to reward them those are all things that  you learn in a training class so even  though i grew up with a dog i still went  to training class with kona every week  for about like three months when we  first got him and it was super helpful  because i learned things like shaping  and positive reinforcement but after  that i got a hang of like what it takes  to train dogs typically i use sort of  the positive reinforcement way of doing  things i never like hit my dogs like  none of that there's a lot of really  great youtube channels actually out  there on how you can train your dog to  do certain tricks or to curb certain  behaviors if you're thinking about  getting a corgi or shiba inu because  those two are really popular dogs that  need honestly a lot of training then  definitely look into it okay so the last  part is really just about general advice  that i have for all of you who are  thinking about getting dogs so having  dogs is definitely one of the most  rewarding and most amazing things like i  honestly think of my dogs as like my  children and i can't imagine a life  without them i have such a strong bond  with both of them genuinely we don't  deserve dogs i love dogs but again i  will caveat this i think one realistic  way to think about whether you're ready  to have dogs is the first two years  especially if you're getting a puppy  maybe a little less so if you're getting  an older dog it's going to require a lot  of patience as you learn what your dog's  needs are and they adjust to your  lifestyle and it's a long-term  commitment dogs live anywhere from eight  to 16 years and so just really think  about whether you can commit to that  time just know that like there's no  one right way to do things but it is  important to know that like  you it takes a lot of patience but if  you work on it it can work but these are  just some of the main lessons that i  want to talk about to dog ownership if  you have any questions leave them in the  comments down below i really like  talking about dogs i can recommend like  dog treats dog toys big chunk of my life  is dogs gonna shake  good boy kind of big  yes good boy good job give me 10.  yes good girl  good job here you go good job guys  you did it  thanks for being in my video youtube  [Music]
 

